{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0446", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-stabilizer}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:91dbadae7da751ff07ed85cd0c3aed0c58e079c16eb4a31497b60081ad51caa8", "source_text": "The stabilizer group algebraic space", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cd55a7afecce359a70f624787eceae88f1a9ab54dfab91ae0c4dea90093399a1", "unit_id": "tag:0446:title"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0446", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{groupoids-section-stabilizer}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7ad5464e30af907bebe0e79306e69608c991be2e515de0f4f54295bbb87268fe", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nPlease compare with\nGroupoids, Section <REF_0001>.\nGiven a groupoid in algebraic spaces we get a group algebraic space as follows.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1bf704f3871ab914134a239194813f9614b9195c932eaeed64d2fbfde3b77c8b", "unit_id": "tag:0446:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0446", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$B \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0003": "$B$", "MATH_0004": "$G$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nG \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & R \\ar[d]^{j = (t, s)} \\\\\nU \\ar[r]^-{\\Delta} & U \\times_B U\n}\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$m$", "MATH_0008": "$c$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-notation}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-groupoid-stabilizer}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2252cdb3d3c649bc0d352f492091cd04ba65921338ec0bf2eecf3c8ea20b449d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9197fa32e6484f5986c9079aff12b9f3b40a057747aeea0ea6250c8605df26f5", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> as in Section <REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a groupoid in algebraic spaces over <MATH_0003>.\nThe algebraic space <MATH_0004> defined by the cartesian square\n<MATH_0005>\nis a group algebraic space over <MATH_0006> with composition law\n<MATH_0007> induced by the composition law <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fa6728a8f1aa8820739241bc6a5d236f8adc6c3f6afb74f1d06d044d307de3bc", "unit_id": "tag:0447:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0446", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3b095524c802b3224c0c748a1c1e6273122924fa2ed6801e30ea21c80658232a", "source_text": "This is true because in a groupoid category the\nset of self maps of any object forms a group.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:83d84b7aadaa265c8c5e1b11bd1d95cc2635f9b686898b3af98d585262f895e2", "unit_id": "tag:0447:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0446", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Delta$", "MATH_0002": "$G = j^{-1}(\\Delta_{U/B})$", "MATH_0003": "$R$", "MATH_0004": "$G = j^{-1}(\\Delta_{U/B}) \\to U$", "MATH_0005": "$s$", "MATH_0006": "$t$", "MATH_0007": "$m$", "MATH_0008": "$c$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c01c7e8dcba6902211e1adfdcefd82022661ebef874225469c1f49d114a4ea34", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6d34fe40b907567c8f84ca73ced60422c469d4c663b499262094961849ede319", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nSince <MATH_0001> is a monomorphism we see that <MATH_0002> is a\nsubsheaf of <MATH_0003>. Thinking of it in this way, the structure morphism\n<MATH_0004> is induced by either <MATH_0005> or <MATH_0006>\n(it is the same), and <MATH_0007> is induced by <MATH_0008>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:57df1b4f44f934aba84b444ce7dcac6f146913f8ab350ecb308baa8677155729", "unit_id": "tag:0446:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0446", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$B \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0003": "$B$", "MATH_0004": "$j^{-1}(\\Delta_{U/B}) \\to U$", "MATH_0005": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-notation}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-stabilizer-groupoid}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7c5310ce4f7ab8df06804ce75832332d40a82a24d306fb23c254013fce47d64d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8b7c72c8b843b65a40f08bd1f9673c2947e05748f8d6d891cef66dbc33bed3c5", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> as in Section <REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a groupoid in algebraic spaces over <MATH_0003>.\nThe group algebraic space <MATH_0004> is called the\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>stabilizer of the groupoid in algebraic spaces <MATH_0005><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:69473c9553b7670333b1c92d6f6b08d9198759ac17c4962ae9d886fb7d56dd1d", "unit_id": "tag:0448:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0446", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3373d69d1a771d1b240d3f94798edce7e161caf54de4b2de49dd8524c8dc1502", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0dd724d3d8aea6e34f3a303bef9bb286dad4e5545a9e05574dd3975c19267464", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn the literature the stabilizer group algebraic space is often denoted <MATH_0001>\n(because the word stabilizer starts with an ``s'' presumably);\nwe cannot do this since we have already used <MATH_0002> for the base scheme.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0c8837f1e31baa79e455b8191dbbe3c750e33da6ccf9bbb89a6d4a55c9b51adb", "unit_id": "tag:0446:prose-0003"}
